WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Speaker 1: I really can't believe this is where&nbsp;
the country is right now, but 30 percent of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:12.080
Republicans, three in 10 Republicans now believe&nbsp;
that Donald Trump is going to be reinstated as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:17.680
president sometime in twenty twenty one. What the&nbsp;
hell is wrong with this country? How are so many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:23.680
people this disconnected from reality? Is anybody&nbsp;
else realizing how much of a red alert disaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:32.000
it is that this many Americans are so ignorant&nbsp;
to think that this is even remotely possible?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.400
Now, before we get to the poll numbers. Let&nbsp;
me give you a little bit of context. Over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:42.800
the last couple of weeks, The New York Times, The&nbsp;
Washington Post, The National Review have reported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.600
that Donald Trump believes and is telling&nbsp;
people that he will be reinstated as president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.440
around August. Now, when initially some people&nbsp;
reacted and said, no, no, that's fake news.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.240
The right wing National Review came out&nbsp;
and said, not only does Trump believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.520
there are multiple Republican senators who believe&nbsp;
that David Perdue believes he'll be reinstated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:07.840
Martha McSally believes she's going to be&nbsp;
reinstated. This is impossible. There is no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.520
reinstatement mechanism. We have a president. We&nbsp;
have a line of succession. The president would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.160
be replaced by the vice president. If anything&nbsp;
happens, then comes the speaker of the House.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.960
For now, Trump is neither. I know earlier this&nbsp;
week, we talked about the possibility Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.440
would run for Congress and then try to become&nbsp;
speaker of the House. But for now, Trump is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:34.080
a former president, is not part of the line of&nbsp;
succession. So one side of this is that Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:40.480
Trump is starting to sort of lay the groundwork&nbsp;
for a violent coup attempt. That's one side of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:47.200
But the other side is the people who believe,&nbsp;
hey, they might just confirm the voter fraud&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.880
and then Trump's back in power. They might&nbsp;
reinstate Donald Trump. And it turns out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:02:00.160
30 percent of Republicans believe Donald Trump&nbsp;
will be reinstated in this calendar year. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:05.840
is from a new Politico morning consult poll from&nbsp;
yesterday which found that most Americans realize,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:13.760
of course, Trump won't be reinstated. But&nbsp;
29 percent of Republicans do think Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:20.960
will end up somehow being president again this&nbsp;
year. Almost just as shocking, quite frankly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:26.240
is that 16 percent of Democrats believe&nbsp;
the same thing. 16 percent of Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:31.600
also believe Donald Trump might be reinstated&nbsp;
or will be reinstated as president this year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:37.600
Please call in. I don't care if you're a Democrat&nbsp;
or a Republican or an independent if you believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.760
Donald Trump is going to be reinstated this year.&nbsp;
Please call into the show next week. I want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.680
hear from you. Please explain to me the mechanism&nbsp;
by which Donald Trump would again be president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:53.680
before the end of the year. How would it happen?&nbsp;
This is essentially as unlikely as Jesus appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:03:00.640
by August. They're essentially equally likely. And&nbsp;
a question that's never answered when you ask them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:08.000
is by what mechanism or legal authority will&nbsp;
Donald Trump be reinstated? What precedent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:14.960
would allow something like this to happen? And&nbsp;
this is how we get back to the coup idea, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:21.040
there is no such mechanism. There is no such&nbsp;
president precedent short of a violent revolution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:26.800
of some kind, which probably requires the backing&nbsp;
of the really the majority of the military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.320
to remove Joe Biden. There is no way that this&nbsp;
could happen. And that's why we keep thinking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:39.840
Are they thinking of some kind of violent coup?&nbsp;
The other aspect about the 30 percent that believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:46.640
that Donald Trump is going to be reinstated&nbsp;
is that 30 percent are willing to admit it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.720
And that's something else we have to think&nbsp;
about. There could be another chunk of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:57.360
electorate that believes Donald Trump is going to&nbsp;
be reinstated this year, but has the sense not to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:03.440
admit it when they're called by a pollster. That's&nbsp;
a possibility for sure. So a substitute headline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.760
would be 30 percent of Republicans willing&nbsp;
to admit they believe Donald Trump will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.720
reinstated. And then another substitute headline&nbsp;
would be 30 percent of Republicans believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.320
anything that comes out of Donald Trump's&nbsp;
mouth period, no matter how absurd it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:23.280
if you go to them in September. And, of&nbsp;
course, Trump won't be president and you say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.480
what happened? Explain what happened.&nbsp;
They will come up with some excuse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:35.440
And if 30 percent believe this, then Donald&nbsp;
Trump surely could get reelected in 2024&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:41.040
because they still love him and they've&nbsp;
learned nothing from the disaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.000
that was the last four years of Donald Trump.&nbsp;
This is really scary stuff. And it's sort of like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:52.560
best case and worst case. Worst case, these people&nbsp;
are just dumb and they don't understand Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:05:01.280
being reinstated is impossible. Worst case, they&nbsp;
understand the idea. Reinstatement as code that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:06.000
they should do some kind of violent coup attempt&nbsp;
and we're going to see real violence coming coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:11.840
up in the end of summer. The best case isn't good,&nbsp;
but the worst case is really significantly worse.

